  "timeout_sec": 30,
  "hints": [
    {
      "tr": "Başlangıç kodunda 1000 baytlık iki farklı mesaj aynı sayıyı verebiliyor.",
      "en": "In the starter code two different 1000-byte messages can give the same number."
    },
    {
      "tr": "`h = hashlib.sha256(message.encode()).digest()`, sonra `int.from_bytes(h, \"big\") % n`.",
      "en": "`h = hashlib.sha256(message.encode()).digest()`, then `int.from_bytes(h, \"big\") % n`."
    },
    {
      "tr": "Çözümün tamamı:\n\n```python\nimport hashlib\n\n\ndef digest(message, n):\n    h = hashlib.sha256(message.encode()).digest()\n    return int.from_bytes(h, \"big\") % n\n\nn = 104723 * 104729\nprint(digest(\"hello\", n) < n)\nprint(digest(\"a\" * 1000, n) == digest(\"a\" * 999 + \"b\", n))\nprint(digest(\"release 2.4.1\", n) == digest(\"release 2.4.1\", n))\n```",
      "en": "The full solution:\n\n```python\nimport hashlib\n\n\ndef digest(message, n):\n    h = hashlib.sha256(message.encode()).digest()\n    return int.from_bytes(h, \"big\") % n\n\nn = 104723 * 104729\nprint(digest(\"hello\", n) < n)\nprint(digest(\"a\" * 1000, n) == digest(\"a\" * 999 + \"b\", n))\nprint(digest(\"release 2.4.1\", n) == digest(\"release 2.4.1\", n))\n```"
    }
  ],
  "checks": [
    {
      "type": "function",
      "name": "digest",
      "cases": [
